/ The editor of an SMS, Push, Teams, Slack or Voice template or campaign:
/ TessEdit with the kit of its transport (app/javascript/nuntius/kits/messages.js),
/ its preview in the middle (TemplatesController#preview, with sample values)
/ and its settings in Inspect. Its controller's assign_design takes the
/ document. Locals: record, name (the form's param key), options (the
/ editor's, e.g. {template: true}), translations_url (optional), slots, the
/ form's own fields for its slot fields.
- problems = %i[text payload from to].flat_map { |attribute| record.errors.full_messages_for(attribute) }
- if problems.any?
  .m-4.rounded-md.border.border-red-200.bg-red-50.px-3.py-2.text-sm.text-red-700 role="alert"
    - problems.each do |problem|
      p = problem
/ An empty variables URL when its class has none, so the variables controller can point it at another
div class="h-[80vh]" data-controller="tess-edit" data-tess-edit-kit-value=record.transport data-tess-edit-sample-value="false" data-tess-edit-frame-value="false" data-tess-edit-variables-url-value=(Nuntius::Variables.url(self, record.variable_roots) || "") data-tess-edit-translations-url-value=local_assigns[:translations_url] data-tess-edit-options-value=options.merge(previewUrl: preview_admin_templates_path).to_json
  = hidden_field_tag "#{name}[design_json]", record.message_document.to_json, id: nil, data: {tess_edit_target: "jsonInput"}
  = slots
